# Task 151-004: Discord Bot Deploy + Smoke Test — Execution Plan

## Scope
- scripts/deploy-discord.sh (new)
- docs/launch/discord-bot-setup.md (new)

## Context
- DiscordConnector is fully implemented in src/connectors/discord.ts (discord.js)
- ConnectorPool manages multi-connector lifecycle (start/stop)
- IncomingMessageRouter routes messages to EventBus → nervous system
- Token stored in .deck secret file as $DECK:DISCORD_TOKEN
- Config: .deckent/config.json connectors.discord section

## Approach

### 1. deploy-discord.sh
A shell script that:
- Checks prerequisites (node, .deck file, discord token set)
- Validates .deckent/config.json has connectors.discord.enabled: true
- Builds the project (tsc check)
- Starts the Discord bot via a Node.js inline runner (uses DiscordConnector + IncomingMessageRouter)
- Outputs status + smoke test instructions

Note: Cannot run npm publish or bot login (no token in CI). Script is written for Alperen to run manually.

### 2. discord-bot-setup.md
Complete setup guide covering:
- Prerequisites
- Discord Developer Portal steps
- .deck file configuration
- .deckent/config.json changes
- Running the deploy script
- Smoke test commands
- Troubleshooting

## Files to create
1. /workspace/scripts/deploy-discord.sh
2. /workspace/docs/launch/discord-bot-setup.md

